/* ===== Wonderland redesign, round 7 (22 November 2026, Charlie): a lighter This Fortnight =====
   This Fortnight had gathered most of the old At a glance as well as What's new, and Charlie was drowning in it. Nothing is
   removed; the same blocks, with their own code, now sit where they belong:
   - This Fortnight keeps what is new: the headline five, What has changed, every update with its filters, and the Spotlight.
   - The Roadmap gains the roadmap's own charts (When will it land?, Where is the change?, What does it touch?) and Coming up,
     between the Curiosity Meter and the roadmap explorer.
   - Governance gains the Duchess's briefing, executive mode (this issue in 90 seconds) and What needs your agency, at the top
     of its front page, above the royal decrees.
   Links, search, Ask Alice, the Curiosity Meter and the tour follow the blocks to their new pages, and a link to any part of
   the issue that is not on the page you are on now opens the page it is on. Executive mode opens on Governance.
   This runs after rd6.js (joined onto rd.js at build time) and uses rd.js's helpers through window.ccRdKit.

   Round 10 (Charlie, 23 Nov 2026): At a glance is back whole. Charlie missed its richness (the Curiosity Meter with what is
   on today and next, Make this issue yours, what has changed, the headline five, the numbers, the Duchess's briefing, What
   needs your agency, the Spotlight, Coming up and every roadmap item), so through the looking-glass it is This Fortnight's first
   page again, in its own order, with its own code; What's new is This Fortnight's second page. The Duchess's briefing, executive
   mode and What needs your agency are back on At a glance, and Governance opens with a card that leads to them. The Roadmap is
   slim: its painting, When will it land?, Where is the change? and What does it touch?, then cards to every roadmap item (on
   At a glance) and On the horizon. Home, the menus and the section front pages work as before.

   Round 11 (Charlie, 23 Nov 2026): on This Fortnight through the looking-glass the Duchess's briefing (This fortnight for Queensland
   agencies) and What needs your agency come straight after Make this issue yours, before What has changed, as the issue's own
   Where do I start? answer puts it. The Pocket Watch and Remind me boxes are not repeated there (Home has both: the Two-Minute
   Briefing and Make this issue yours) and the Spotlight on the Cowork scenarios is not shown (Curious tools on This Fortnight in the
   garden tells it). The tour, the menus' parts and search follow (rd.js r11order and r11off; rd.css round 11). */
